    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48485" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŏlētum</span></b> , i,
			n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Spain</i>, now <i>Toledo</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 35,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">39, 30</span></i>.
			— Hence, adj.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŏlētānus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>of Toletum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">culter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Grat. Cyn. 34</span></i>
			. — As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŏlētāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Toletum</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 35,
			22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 3, 4, § 25</span></i>.</div>
